; The only zone dns-decoy serves.
;
; Its existence is what makes NS_DELEGATION_LAME real: dns-decoy is genuinely
; authoritative for *something*, so when test.zone delegates lame.test to it, it
; answers REFUSED immediately rather than timing out or returning SERVFAIL for a
; different reason. An empty server would not reproduce the same condition.
$ORIGIN decoy.test.
$TTL 300

@       IN SOA  ns-decoy.test. hostmaster.propgate.invalid. (
                1 7200 3600 1209600 300 )
@       IN NS   ns-decoy.test.
@       IN TXT  "i am authoritative for decoy.test and nothing else"
